+## Routes
+
+- `POST /import/sales` takes `{ "csv": "..." }` with the columns
+  `ticket,soldAt,dishId,qty` (`soldAt` is an ISO instant). Each dish sold
+  uses one portion of its recipe per `qty`; the ingredients are consumed at
+  `soldAt` with the ledger `ref` `sale:<ticket>`. Tickets already imported
+  are skipped. If a row is invalid or an item runs out, nothing is imported
+  and the `bad_request` message names the row (`row 2` is the first data
+  row). Answers `{ "tickets": <count>, "dishes": <count> }`, where `dishes`
+  is the total `qty` imported.
+- `GET /reports/variance?from=YYYY-MM-DD&to=YYYY-MM-DD` lists per item
+  `{ itemId, name, unit, theoretical, actual, difference }`: theoretical use
+  from sales sold in those days (inclusive), actual use from every `consume`
+  movement in them, and `difference` = actual − theoretical. Items where
+  both are zero are left out.
